{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN3KbbPdC8P1JeUZR7A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the integration, but I haven't tested it against the real Intervals.icu. That needs the real client credentials. The only check I ran was a quick one on the new `state` token (valid, tampered and expired cases).\n\nFour causes, now written up in `ANSWER.md`:\n\n1. **Connect failed for everyone.** The button was a plain link to a GET endpoint, and a page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header. Init is now an authenticated POST that returns `{authorize_url}`, and `static/app.js` navigates to it.\n2. **Authorize step returned `invalid_request`.** The scope named `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` as both READ and WRITE since the calendar sync shipped. It's now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`, in `config.py`.\n3. **Rivera was told to reconnect after an hour.** The code assumed a 3600-second token lifetime and expired the connection. Intervals tokens don't expire, so I removed that and the background refresher. A 401 from Intervals now clears the token and shows \"reconnect\".\n4. **Token exchange sent extra fields.** It now sends only `client_id`, `client_secret` and `code`.\n\nI also made `state` a signed token with a user id, a purpose and a 15-minute expiry. A reconnect with a different Intervals athlete than the one stored is now rejected.\n\nStill open:\n- The token sits in the in-memory store unencrypted. The standard library has no cipher, so encrypting it at rest is left for the real database; there's a note in `store_connection`.\n- `APP_SECRET` and the client secret in `config.py` are still the dev placeholders.\n\nI didn't commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":142,"cache_read_input_tokens":33433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_